update events set lead='Santa rides from Circular Quay to Martin Place with a 90-piece marching band and elves on reindeer tricycles, then helps the Lord Mayor light Sydney''s 24-metre tree, followed by fireworks.', about='Sydney''s Christmas season begins on Thursday 26 November with Santa''s sleigh ride and the lighting of the Martin Place Christmas tree, from 6.30pm to 8.30pm.

Santa''s sleigh leaves Customs House Square at Circular Quay at 8.05pm and travels along Pitt Street to Martin Place, joined by the 90-piece NSW Public Schools Millennium Marching Band and elves on reindeer tricycles. At about 8.30pm, Lord Mayor Clover Moore AO helps Santa light the 24-metre tree, decorated with designs inspired by Australian flowers, followed by fireworks.

It''s free. DJs and roving entertainers play at both ends of the route from 6.30pm. There are no food trucks in Martin Place, so eat nearby or bring snacks, and use public transport.', story='[{"type": "text", "text": "On the last Thursday in November, Santa comes to the city in style. His sleigh sets off from Customs House Square at Circular Quay and travels along Pitt Street to Martin Place, where he helps the Lord Mayor switch on Sydney''s Christmas tree."}, {"type": "image", "url": "/images/library/unsplash-abishanth-ahilan-fireworks.jpg", "alt": "Golden fireworks against a dark night sky", "layout": "right", "caption": "Stand-in photo: Abishanth Ahilan. Santa''s Sydney Sleigh Ride and Tree Lighting photos coming soon"}, {"type": "text", "text": "From 6.30pm, DJ Mimi Velevska and roving entertainers warm up the crowd at Customs House Square, while DJ Sheba Williams plays at Martin Place. The elves arrive at Customs House Square at 7.25pm, and the NSW Public Schools Millennium Marching Band plays a trumpet fanfare at 8pm. At 8.05pm the sleigh departs with Santa and the Lord Mayor, accompanied by the 90-piece band and elves on reindeer tricycles.", "heading": "The sleigh ride"}, {"type": "text", "text": "The sleigh reaches Martin Place at about 8.25pm. At 8.30pm, Lord Mayor Clover Moore AO helps Santa light the 24-metre tree, its decorations inspired by Australian flowers, and fireworks light up the sky. After the lighting, the tree''s colours change every 15 minutes until midnight.", "heading": "Tree lighting and fireworks"}, {"type": "text", "text": "You can walk alongside the route, but no one can ride on the sleigh with Santa. There are no food or drink trucks in Martin Place, so grab dinner nearby or bring snacks. Public transport is the easiest way in and out.", "heading": "Know before you go"}]'::jsonb, highlights='[{"title": "24-metre tree", "detail": "Lit at 8.30pm"}, {"title": "90-piece band", "detail": "Leading Santa''s sleigh"}, {"title": "Free", "detail": "Fireworks to finish"}]'::jsonb, good_to_know='["Free", "Sleigh leaves Customs House Square at 8.05pm", "Tree lighting and fireworks at Martin Place at 8.30pm", "No food trucks in Martin Place: eat nearby or bring snacks", "Use public transport: transportnsw.info or 131 500", "The tree''s colours change every 15 minutes until midnight"]'::jsonb, venue_about='Martin Place is the pedestrian plaza at the heart of Sydney''s CBD, home to the city''s Christmas tree each December.', maps_url='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Martin%20Place%2C%20Sydney%20NSW%202000', updated_at=now() where slug='santas-sydney-sleigh-ride-tree-lighting';
update events set end_date='2026-12-24', time_text='Nightly from 1 December', lead='A different choir sings carols beside Sydney''s 24-metre Christmas tree in Martin Place every night in the lead-up to Christmas.', about='From Tuesday 1 December, a different choir sings carols beside the Christmas tree in Martin Place every night in the lead-up to Christmas, part of the City of Sydney''s Christmas program.

The 24-metre tree, decorated with designs inspired by Australian flowers, makes a beautiful backdrop, and its lights change colour every 15 minutes after dark.

Performances are free. Check the City of Sydney''s What''s On page for each night''s choir and time.', story='[{"type": "text", "text": "Every evening in December, Martin Place takes on the feel of a village square at Christmas. From 1 December, a different choir sings carols beside the city''s 24-metre Christmas tree, every night in the lead-up to Christmas."}, {"type": "image", "url": "/images/library/unsplash-aaron-burden-silent-night.jpg", "alt": "Open song book on the Silent Night page with warm lights behind", "layout": "right", "caption": "Stand-in photo: Aaron Burden. Choirs in the City photos coming soon"}, {"type": "text", "text": "Stop on the way home from work, or plan an evening in the city around it. The tree''s decorations are inspired by Australian flowers, and after dark its lights change colour every 15 minutes, so stay a little while after the singing ends.", "heading": "Stay for the lights"}]'::jsonb, highlights='[{"title": "Every night", "detail": "From 1 December"}, {"title": "Free", "detail": "In Martin Place"}, {"title": "24-metre tree", "detail": "The backdrop for the carols"}]'::jsonb, good_to_know='["Free", "A different choir each night from 1 December", "Check the City of Sydney What''s On page for times", "Pair it with the Martin Place tree lights, which change every 15 minutes"]'::jsonb, maps_url='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Martin%20Place%2C%20Sydney%20NSW%202000', updated_at=now() where slug='choirs-in-the-city-martin-place';
update events set lead='Crown Street closes to traffic for a free day of Christmas music, salsa, a dog parade, Santa''s sleigh ride and photos, and The Grinch on an outdoor screen.', about='The Surry Hills Christmas Fair takes over Crown Street, between Cleveland and Foveaux streets, on Saturday 12 December from 12pm to 10pm. The street is closed to traffic, and three zones run from 12pm to 9pm.

The Jingle Jam Stage at Collins Street Reserve, beside the Surry Hills Christmas tree, hosts live music and Christmas line dancing, starting with the Santa Paws Dog Parade at 12pm, hosted by Hannah Conda. The Tinsel Showtime Garden at Tudor Street Reserve has live entertainment and festive food, and The Festive Hub at Shannon Reserve has games and activities.

Santa''s sleigh rides down Crown Street from 2pm, Santa photos run from 3pm to 9pm for a $5 donation to Variety – the Children''s Charity, and The Grinch screens outdoors at 7pm. Entry is free.', story='[{"type": "text", "text": "For one Saturday in December, Crown Street belongs to pedestrians. The Surry Hills Christmas Fair closes the street between Cleveland and Foveaux streets from 12pm to 10pm, with three zones of music, food and festive fun."}, {"type": "image", "url": "/images/library/unsplash-josh-hild-market.jpg", "alt": "Festive street market under lit trees", "layout": "right", "caption": "Stand-in photo: Josh Hild. Surry Hills Christmas Fair photos coming soon"}, {"type": "text", "text": "The day begins at the Jingle Jam Stage at Collins Street Reserve, beside the Surry Hills Christmas tree, with the Santa Paws Dog Parade from 12pm to 1pm, hosted by drag performer Hannah Conda, with prizes for the best-dressed dogs and owners. The Holly Jolly Stage plays Christmas music all day, with salsa performances and beginner salsa lessons from 5pm.", "heading": "A dog parade and dancing in the street"}, {"type": "text", "text": "At 2pm, Santa''s sleigh travels down Crown Street from Cleveland Street to the Surry Hills Christmas tree. Santa photos run at The Festive Hub in Shannon Reserve from 3pm to 9pm for a $5 donation to Variety – the Children''s Charity, and the Variety stall offers face painting and coloured hair spray for a donation.", "heading": "Santa''s sleigh and photos"}, {"type": "text", "text": "As night falls, The Grinch screens outdoors at The Festive Hub at 7pm, with live captions. There''s a quiet space, accessible toilets and guest assistance. Central station is the nearest train and metro stop, and the Surry Hills light rail stop on Devonshire Street is close by.", "heading": "Movie night and getting there"}]'::jsonb, highlights='[{"title": "Free", "detail": "12pm to 10pm"}, {"title": "Santa Paws", "detail": "Dog parade at 12pm"}, {"title": "The Grinch", "detail": "Outdoor screening at 7pm"}]'::jsonb, good_to_know='["Free entry; Crown Street is closed to traffic", "Santa photos 3pm to 9pm, $5 donation to Variety", "Santa''s sleigh ride at 2pm", "Outdoor screening of The Grinch at 7pm, with live captions", "Quiet space, accessible toilets and guest assistance", "Nearest station: Central; light rail: Surry Hills"]'::jsonb, maps_url='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Crown%20Street%2C%20Surry%20Hills%20NSW%202010', updated_at=now() where slug='surry-hills-christmas-fair';
update events set time_text='8pm–9.30pm (doors 7pm)', price_text='$25.50 adults, $20 concession', official_url='https://whatson.cityofsydney.nsw.gov.au/events/christmas-at-sydney-town-hall', lead='A Christmas spectacular of carols and festive music in Sydney Town Hall, with choirs, harp, the NSW Police Band and the Town Hall''s grand organ.', about='Christmas at Sydney Town Hall is a concert of carols and festive music on Tuesday 15 December, telling the Christmas story through carols and pageantry. Doors open at 7pm and the performance runs from 8pm to 9.30pm.

Choirs, harp, the NSW Police Band and Sydney Town Hall''s grand organ fill the building. The concert is produced by organist, conductor and composer Titus Grenyer, who also produces the City of Sydney''s organ recitals at the Town Hall.

Tickets are $25.50 for adults and $20 concession, general admission in the great hall or the galleries. It suits the whole family.', story='[{"type": "text", "text": "Few places in Sydney feel as grand at Christmas as the Town Hall. On Tuesday 15 December, its great hall fills with carols and festive music for Christmas at Sydney Town Hall, a concert that tells the Christmas story through song and pageantry."}, {"type": "image", "url": "/images/library/unsplash-aaron-burden-silent-night.jpg", "alt": "Open song book on the Silent Night page with warm lights behind", "layout": "right", "caption": "Stand-in photo: Aaron Burden. Christmas at Sydney Town Hall photos coming soon"}, {"type": "text", "text": "Choirs and harp join the NSW Police Band and the Town Hall''s grand organ. The concert is produced by Titus Grenyer, an organist, conductor and composer who manages the organ and carillon at the University of Sydney and produces the City of Sydney''s organ recital program at the Town Hall.", "heading": "Choirs, harp and the grand organ"}, {"type": "text", "text": "Doors open at 7pm and the concert runs from 8pm to 9.30pm. Tickets are general admission, with seating in the great hall on the ground floor or in the galleries. Guests who need assisted access should use the lower ground entrance on Druitt Street; both levels have lift access.", "heading": "Tickets and access"}]'::jsonb, highlights='[{"title": "$25.50", "detail": "$20 concession"}, {"title": "Grand organ", "detail": "Plus choirs, harp and the NSW Police Band"}, {"title": "Family friendly", "detail": "8pm to 9.30pm"}]'::jsonb, good_to_know='["Tickets: $25.50 adults, $20 concession", "General admission: great hall or galleries", "Doors 7pm, concert 8pm to 9.30pm", "Assisted access via the Druitt Street lower ground entrance; lifts to both levels", "Suitable for the whole family", "City of Sydney: 02 9265 9333"]'::jsonb, venue_about='Sydney Town Hall, on George Street, is one of the city''s grandest Victorian buildings, home to one of the world''s great concert organs.', maps_url='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Sydney%20Town%20Hall%2C%20483%20George%20Street%2C%20Sydney%20NSW%202000', updated_at=now() where slug='christmas-at-sydney-town-hall';
update events set lead='Melbourne''s best-loved Christmas tradition returns for its 71st season: animated window displays on Bourke Street to wander past with the family, free.', about='The Myer Christmas windows on Bourke Street Mall return for their 71st season, with a new festive theme. The animated displays are one of Melbourne''s most loved Christmas traditions, and they''re on until 5 January.

They''re free to visit any time. Go early in the morning or later in the evening to avoid the busiest queues, and combine your visit with Christmas Square at Fed Square, a short walk away.', story='[{"type": "text", "text": "For more than seven decades, families have queued along Bourke Street to see the Myer Christmas windows. This year marks the 71st season, with a new festive theme brought to life in animated scenes behind the glass."}, {"type": "image", "url": "/images/library/unsplash-cmophoto-carousel.jpg", "alt": "Lit carousel at night decorated for Christmas", "layout": "right", "caption": "Stand-in photo: cmophoto.net. Myer Christmas Windows photos coming soon"}, {"type": "text", "text": "The windows are free to visit and on display until 5 January. The busiest times are weekend afternoons and school holidays, so go early or late for a closer look. Fed Square''s Christmas Square, with the city''s Christmas tree, is a short walk away.", "heading": "Plan your visit"}]'::jsonb, highlights='[{"title": "71st season", "detail": "A Melbourne tradition"}, {"title": "Free", "detail": "Any time"}, {"title": "Until 5 January", "detail": "On Bourke Street Mall"}]'::jsonb, good_to_know='["Free", "On until 5 January", "Go early or late to avoid the queues", "Combine with Christmas Square at Fed Square"]'::jsonb, maps_url='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Myer%20Melbourne%2C%20314%20Bourke%20Street%2C%20Melbourne%20VIC%203000', updated_at=now() where slug='myer-christmas-windows';
update events set lead='The moment Christmas begins in Melbourne: the city''s tree is lit at Fed Square on 27 November, opening Christmas Square for the season.', about='Melbourne''s Christmas celebrations begin on 27 November, when the city''s Christmas tree is lit at Federation Square. The lighting opens Christmas Square, which stays open until 25 December.

It''s free. Check the City of Melbourne''s What''s On page for times and entertainment closer to the date.', story='[{"type": "text", "text": "On 27 November, Melbourne switches into Christmas mode. The city''s Christmas tree is lit at Federation Square, and Christmas Square opens around it for the season."}, {"type": "image", "url": "/images/library/unsplash-abishanth-ahilan-fireworks.jpg", "alt": "Golden fireworks against a dark night sky", "layout": "right", "caption": "Stand-in photo: Abishanth Ahilan. Christmas Tree Lighting at Fed Square photos coming soon"}, {"type": "text", "text": "The lighting is free. After the night, Christmas Square stays open until 25 December, and the Myer windows on Bourke Street and the Crown Christmas River Show on the Yarra are close by.", "heading": "After the lighting"}]'::jsonb, highlights='[{"title": "27 November", "detail": "Christmas begins in Melbourne"}, {"title": "Free", "detail": "At Fed Square"}, {"title": "Christmas Square", "detail": "Open until 25 December"}]'::jsonb, good_to_know='["Free", "Check the City of Melbourne What''s On page for times", "Christmas Square stays open until 25 December"]'::jsonb, maps_url='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Federation%20Square%2C%20Swanston%20Street%2C%20Melbourne%20VIC%203000', updated_at=now() where slug='melbourne-christmas-tree-lighting';
update events set lead='Fed Square becomes Melbourne''s Christmas meeting place from 27 November to Christmas Day, centred on the city''s Christmas tree.', about='Christmas Square turns Federation Square into a festive meeting place from 27 November to 25 December, centred on Melbourne''s Christmas tree.

It''s an easy stop while you''re in the city for Christmas shopping, the Myer windows on Bourke Street or the Crown Christmas River Show on the Yarra.', story='[{"type": "text", "text": "From 27 November until Christmas Day, Federation Square becomes Christmas Square, a festive gathering place built around Melbourne''s Christmas tree."}, {"type": "image", "url": "/images/library/unsplash-cmophoto-carousel.jpg", "alt": "Lit carousel at night decorated for Christmas", "layout": "right", "caption": "Stand-in photo: cmophoto.net. Christmas Square at Fed Square photos coming soon"}, {"type": "text", "text": "Pair it with the other City of Melbourne Christmas favourites nearby: the Myer windows on Bourke Street, sparkly decorations around the city, the Crown Christmas River Show on the Yarra from 4 December, and the Christmas Carnival at Birrarung Marr from 11 December.", "heading": "Make a day of it"}]'::jsonb, highlights='[{"title": "27 Nov – 25 Dec", "detail": "Daily"}, {"title": "City tree", "detail": "At the heart of the square"}, {"title": "In the city", "detail": "Near the Myer windows"}]'::jsonb, good_to_know='["Open 27 November to 25 December", "Combine with the Myer Christmas windows on Bourke Street", "Crown Christmas River Show on the Yarra from 4 December"]'::jsonb, maps_url='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Federation%20Square%2C%20Swanston%20Street%2C%20Melbourne%20VIC%203000', updated_at=now() where slug='melbourne-christmas-square';
update events set lead='A free water, laser and light show on the Yarra River every night from 4 to 25 December.', about='The Crown Christmas River Show lights up the Yarra River with water, lasers and light from 4 to 25 December, part of the City of Melbourne''s Christmas program.

It''s free. Check the City of Melbourne''s What''s On page for nightly show times.', story='[{"type": "text", "text": "After dark in December, the Yarra becomes a stage. The Crown Christmas River Show combines water, lasers and light in a free show on the river, running from 4 to 25 December."}, {"type": "image", "url": "/images/library/unsplash-abishanth-ahilan-fireworks.jpg", "alt": "Golden fireworks against a dark night sky", "layout": "right", "caption": "Stand-in photo: Abishanth Ahilan. Crown Christmas River Show photos coming soon"}, {"type": "text", "text": "Find a spot along the riverbank and stay for a show after dinner in the city. The Christmas Carnival at Birrarung Marr, also on the Yarra, runs from 11 to 24 December.", "heading": "Make a night of it"}]'::jsonb, highlights='[{"title": "Free", "detail": "Nightly"}, {"title": "4 – 25 Dec", "detail": "On the Yarra River"}, {"title": "Water, lasers, light", "detail": "A Christmas river show"}]'::jsonb, good_to_know='["Free", "Nightly from 4 to 25 December", "Check show times on the City of Melbourne What''s On page"]'::jsonb, maps_url='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Southbank%20Promenade%2C%20Melbourne%20VIC', updated_at=now() where slug='crown-christmas-river-show';
update events set lead='Thrill rides, carnival games and festive food on the banks of the Yarra at Birrarung Marr, from 11 to 24 December.', about='The Christmas Carnival sets up on the banks of the Yarra at Birrarung Marr from 11 to 24 December, part of the City of Melbourne''s Christmas program, with thrill rides, carnival games and festive food.

Entry is free; rides and games may cost extra. Check the City of Melbourne''s What''s On page for opening hours.', story='[{"type": "text", "text": "In the final fortnight before Christmas, the riverside park at Birrarung Marr fills with lights and music for the Christmas Carnival, running from 11 to 24 December."}, {"type": "image", "url": "/images/library/unsplash-engin-akyurt-ferris-wheel.jpg", "alt": "Ferris wheel lit up at night at a carnival", "layout": "right", "caption": "Stand-in photo: engin akyurt. Christmas Carnival at Birrarung Marr photos coming soon"}, {"type": "text", "text": "Expect thrill rides, carnival games and festive food on the banks of the Yarra. Entry is free, though rides and games may cost extra. Fed Square''s Christmas Square is a short walk away.", "heading": "Rides, games and festive food"}]'::jsonb, highlights='[{"title": "11 – 24 Dec", "detail": "Birrarung Marr"}, {"title": "Free entry", "detail": "Rides and games may cost extra"}, {"title": "Thrill rides", "detail": "And carnival games"}]'::jsonb, good_to_know='["Free entry; rides and games may cost extra", "On from 11 to 24 December", "Check opening hours on the City of Melbourne What''s On page", "A short walk from Fed Square"]'::jsonb, maps_url='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Birrarung%20Marr%2C%20Melbourne%20VIC%203000', updated_at=now() where slug='melbourne-christmas-carnival';
update events set lead='Adelaide lights its brand-new 25-metre Christmas tree in Victoria Square / Tarntanyangga, with Gospo Collective, L.I.L.L.I, Adelaide Afrobeat Collective and food trucks.', about='Adelaide''s new 25-metre Christmas tree is lit for the first time in Victoria Square / Tarntanyangga on Saturday 21 November, from 6pm to 9pm, with the lighting at about 8.30pm.

MC Shanelle Franklin hosts performances from Gospo Collective, L.I.L.L.I, Adelaide Afrobeat Collective and The Cast. Food trucks are on site; bring a picnic blanket.

The free event opens Adelaide''s Christmas Festival. The new artificial tree, made by an Australian company, replaces the square''s old tree and is designed to look good by day as well as night.', story='[{"type": "text", "text": "Victoria Square / Tarntanyangga welcomes a brand-new Christmas tree this year. The 25-metre tree is lit for the first time on Saturday 21 November, opening the City of Adelaide''s Christmas Festival."}, {"type": "image", "url": "/images/library/unsplash-abishanth-ahilan-fireworks.jpg", "alt": "Golden fireworks against a dark night sky", "layout": "right", "caption": "Stand-in photo: Abishanth Ahilan. Christmas Tree Lighting in Victoria Square photos coming soon"}, {"type": "text", "text": "From 6pm, MC Shanelle Franklin introduces performances from Gospo Collective, L.I.L.L.I, Adelaide Afrobeat Collective and The Cast. Food trucks keep everyone fed, so bring a picnic blanket and settle in. The tree is lit at about 8.30pm.", "heading": "Music and food trucks"}, {"type": "text", "text": "The new tree, an artificial tree made by an Australian company, replaces the old tree that had stood in the square for years. It''s designed to look good in daylight as well as after dark, and it stays up through the festive season.", "heading": "A new tree for the city"}]'::jsonb, highlights='[{"title": "New 25m tree", "detail": "Lit for the first time"}, {"title": "Free", "detail": "6pm to 9pm"}, {"title": "Live music", "detail": "Gospo Collective, L.I.L.L.I and more"}]'::jsonb, good_to_know='["Free", "Tree lighting at about 8.30pm", "Food trucks on site", "Bring a picnic blanket", "Opens Adelaide''s Christmas Festival"]'::jsonb, maps_url='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Victoria%20Square%20/%20Tarntanyangga%2C%20Adelaide%20SA%205000', updated_at=now() where slug='adelaide-christmas-tree-lighting';
update events set lead='Light Square becomes an open-air cinema for a free screening of Elf, with DJ WiPod, escape puzzles from Fox in a Box and Christmas elves before the film.', about='Light Square / Wauwi turns into an open-air cinema on Friday 4 December for a free screening of Elf, starring Will Ferrell, part of Adelaide''s Christmas Festival.

Things get going from 5pm with DJ WiPod, escape puzzles and games from Fox in a Box Adelaide, and Christmas elves. Food and drink are available to buy, and the film starts at sundown.

Entry is free; registration is recommended. Bring a picnic rug.', story='[{"type": "text", "text": "On the first Friday in December, Light Square / Wauwi becomes an outdoor cinema for one of the best-loved Christmas films of all. Wauwi Nights screens Elf, starring Will Ferrell, free under the stars."}, {"type": "image", "url": "/images/library/unsplash-hamideh-jafari-decorated-cookies.jpg", "alt": "Tray of iced Christmas tree cookies", "layout": "right", "caption": "Stand-in photo: Hamideh Jafari. Wauwi Nights: Elf photos coming soon"}, {"type": "text", "text": "From 5pm, DJ WiPod sets the mood, Fox in a Box Adelaide brings escape puzzles and games, and Christmas elves roam the square. Food and drink are available to buy, so come early, spread out a picnic rug and settle in before the film starts at sundown.", "heading": "Games, elves and a DJ"}]'::jsonb, highlights='[{"title": "Free", "detail": "Registration recommended"}, {"title": "Elf", "detail": "Starts at sundown"}, {"title": "From 5pm", "detail": "DJ, games and elves"}]'::jsonb, good_to_know='["Free; registration recommended", "Activities from 5pm, film at sundown", "Food and drink available to buy", "Bring a picnic rug"]'::jsonb, maps_url='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Light%20Square%20/%20Wauwi%2C%20Adelaide%20SA%205000', updated_at=now() where slug='wauwi-nights-elf';
update events set address='Melbourne Street, North Adelaide (corner of Melbourne and Jerningham streets)', price_text='Free entry', lead='More than 75 artisan stalls line Melbourne Street in North Adelaide, with free Father Christmas photos, a pop-up Christmas choir, live music and street food.', about='Meander Market brings more than 75 artisan stalls to Melbourne Street, North Adelaide, on Saturday 5 December, from 10am to 3pm.

Father Christmas is there for free photos from 10.30am to 1pm. There''s live music, a pop-up Christmas choir, face painting, caricatures and street food.

Entry is free. It''s part of Adelaide''s Christmas Festival.', story='[{"type": "text", "text": "Melbourne Street in North Adelaide becomes a Christmas market on Saturday 5 December, with more than 75 artisan stalls stretching from the corner of Jerningham Street."}, {"type": "image", "url": "/images/library/unsplash-josh-hild-market.jpg", "alt": "Festive street market under lit trees", "layout": "right", "caption": "Stand-in photo: Josh Hild. Meander Market Christmas photos coming soon"}, {"type": "text", "text": "Father Christmas is there for free photos from 10.30am to 1pm. A pop-up Christmas choir and live music set the mood, children can have their faces painted or sit for a caricature, and street food vendors keep everyone fed.", "heading": "Free photos with Father Christmas"}]'::jsonb, highlights='[{"title": "75+ stalls", "detail": "Artisan gifts"}, {"title": "Free photos", "detail": "Father Christmas, 10.30am to 1pm"}, {"title": "Free entry", "detail": "10am to 3pm"}]'::jsonb, good_to_know='["Free entry", "Father Christmas photos 10.30am to 1pm, free", "Pop-up Christmas choir and live music", "Face painting and caricatures", "Street food"]'::jsonb, maps_url='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Melbourne%20Street%20and%20Jerningham%20Street%2C%20North%20Adelaide%20SA%205006', updated_at=now() where slug='meander-market-north-adelaide';
update events set price_text='$2 entry, under 5s free', lead='More than 100 local market stalls, 20-plus food and drink trucks, a South Australian bar and a free kids'' zone with Father Christmas in Victoria Square / Tarntanyangga.', about='The Adelady Christmas Village sets up in Victoria Square / Tarntanyangga on Friday 11 December from 4pm to 10pm and Saturday 12 December from 12pm to 10pm.

More than 100 local market stalls, more than 20 food and drink trucks and the Bickford''s Group Bar, serving South Australian wines, beers and gins, fill the square. A community stage has DJs, live performances and acoustic sets, and the free kids'' zone has Father Christmas, face painting, letters to Santa and a 360-degree photo booth.

Entry is $2, and free for children under 5. Disabled access is available.', story='[{"type": "text", "text": "For two days in December, Victoria Square / Tarntanyangga becomes a Christmas village. Adelady''s market runs on Friday 11 December from 4pm to 10pm and Saturday 12 December from 12pm to 10pm, supported by the City of Adelaide."}, {"type": "image", "url": "/images/library/unsplash-josh-hild-market.jpg", "alt": "Festive street market under lit trees", "layout": "right", "caption": "Stand-in photo: Josh Hild. Adelady Christmas Village photos coming soon"}, {"type": "text", "text": "More than 100 local market stalls make it easy to find gifts made in South Australia, and more than 20 food and drink trucks have dinner covered. The Bickford''s Group Bar pours South Australian wines, beers and gins, and the community stage has DJs, live performances and acoustic sets.", "heading": "100 stalls and a South Australian bar"}, {"type": "text", "text": "The free kids'' zone has Father Christmas, face painting, letters to Santa and a 360-degree spinning photo booth. Entry to the village is $2, and children under 5 are free.", "heading": "For the kids"}]'::jsonb, highlights='[{"title": "100+ stalls", "detail": "Local makers"}, {"title": "$2 entry", "detail": "Under 5s free"}, {"title": "Free kids'' zone", "detail": "With Father Christmas"}]'::jsonb, good_to_know='["$2 entry; children under 5 free", "Friday 4pm to 10pm, Saturday 12pm to 10pm", "20+ food and drink trucks and a bar", "Free kids'' zone with Father Christmas", "Public toilets; disabled access available"]'::jsonb, maps_url='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Victoria%20Square%20/%20Tarntanyangga%2C%20Adelaide%20SA%205000', updated_at=now() where slug='adelady-christmas-village';
update events set lead='Meet Santa and join in Christmas activities at Santa''s Village in The Darwin Galleria on Smith Street, through November and December.', about='Santa''s Village at The Darwin Galleria on Smith Street runs through November and December as part of Christmas in Darwin. Families can meet Santa and join in festive activities, from 9am to 1.30pm.

